# ==================================================
# Brisart Research Archive
# Pure Python / Local First / Dependency Free
# Single root .gitignore
# ==================================================
#
# Purpose
# -------
# Exclude generated tooling artifacts, local application state,
# build products, caches, and sensitive runtime material.
# Preserve authored research, source code, documentation, curriculum,
# published evidence, and intentionally archived media.
#
# Communication / relationships
# -----------------------------
# Shared artifact rules cover tools that write into selected projects.
# Project-specific rules are anchored to their owning archive folders.
# Project Context Helper export filters are separate from Git policy:
# exclusion from a text export does not imply exclusion from Git.
#
# Settings / parameters
# ---------------------
# Unanchored artifact names apply at any depth.
# Leading "/" anchors a rule to the archive root.
# Project-scoped "**/" patterns cover nested release lines.
# Trailing "/" restricts a pattern to directories.
#
# Edge cases
# ----------
# Do not globally ignore data/, records/, reports/, results/, models/,
# exports/, state/, packages/, storage/, modules/, or extensions/.
# These names can identify authored content or implementation packages.
# Do not globally ignore JSON, CSV, Markdown, ZIP, PDF, or audio files.
# Do not globally ignore *.lock: dependency lockfiles can be source.
#
# Known limitations
# -----------------
# Ignore rules do not remove files already tracked by Git.
# Ignore rules are not access controls, encryption, or secret scanning.
# Custom output locations require explicit rules when not covered here.
# Files written outside this repository are outside this policy.
# A filename cannot establish whether its contents contain secrets.
#
# Examples
# --------
# Ignored: PROJECT_CONTEXT_EXPORTS/<timestamp>/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md
# Ignored: 98_Tooling/ProjectContextHelper/last_export_settings.json
# Ignored: 95_Identity_Tools/main/vault/data/private_record.json
# Preserved: 97_Encryption/results/research_test_results.json
# Preserved: 98_Tooling/CanonSync/canon/gitignore.master
# Preserved: authored audio/, docs/, tests/, fixtures/, and curriculum.
#
# ==================================================
# 1. GLOBAL DEVELOPMENT ARTIFACTS
# ==================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode and interpreter caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python packaging and build products
#
# Build specifications are intentionally not ignored globally.
# A maintained *.spec file can be part of a reproducible build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
*.egg
*.whl
pip-wheel-metadata/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated native binaries and libraries
#
# Authored C/C++/assembly source remains trackable.
# Deliberately archived binary fixtures require explicit exceptions.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*
*.pyd
*.dylib
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.ilk

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test runners, coverage, static analysis, and development caches
#
# These rules cover development tools, not application dependencies.
# Do not blanket-ignore tests/, fixtures/, vectors/, or results/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pyre/
.pytype/
.hypothesis/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.pybuilder/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtual environments and local dependency installations
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
__pypackages__/
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and IDEs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.vs/
.spyproject/
.ropeproject/
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~
.#*
\#*#
*.sublime-workspace

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating-system metadata
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100/
.Trashes/
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Office application lock files
#
# Actual Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and PDF documents remain trackable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
~$*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local environment secrets
#
# Keep deliberately authored example/template files trackable.
# Do not put real credentials into those examples.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template
!.env.*.example
!.env.*.sample
!.env.*.template
.envrc.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private-key containers and common private-key filenames
#
# Public certificates (*.crt, *.cer, *.pub) are not globally excluded.
# PEM files can contain private keys, so exclude them conservatively.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
private_key.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Disposable caches and temporary files
#
# No global logs/, *.log, *.db, or *.sqlite rules:
# those can also be intentional research or test artifacts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.cache/
*.tmp
*.temp
*.part
*.partial
*.crdownload
*.download
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# SQLite transient sidecars, not the primary database itself.
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-wal
*.db-journal
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# ==================================================
# 2. SHARED BRISART TOOLING ARTIFACTS
#
# These tools can write into arbitrary selected project folders.
# Their distinctive artifact names therefore apply at any depth.
# ==================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project Context Helper
#
# Export bundles, generated context, machine preferences, profiles,
# history, and export-state files belong together in this section.
# No separate last_export_settings.json rule is needed at the bottom.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROJECT_CONTEXT_EXPORTS/
PROJECT_CONTEXT.md
PROJECT_CONTEXT_SETTINGS.json
PROJECT_MANIFEST.json
PROJECT_SUMMARY.txt
PROJECT_SNAPSHOT.zip

# Project Context Helper machine-local application state.
app_settings.json
build_history.json
custom_profiles.json
last_export_settings.json

# Explicit recovery copies of machine-local state.
app_settings.json.bak
build_history.json.bak
custom_profiles.json.bak
last_export_settings.json.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ArchiveSnapshot
#
# Ignore snapshot stores and machine-local automation state.
# Snapshot contents are covered by their containing store directory.
# Do not globally ignore HASHES.sha256, FOLDER_TREE.txt,
# ARCHIVE_MANIFEST.json, or ARCHIVE_SUMMARY.md: those names can also
# identify intentionally published archival records.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARCHIVE_SNAPSHOT/
ARCHIVE_TIMELINE/

ARCHIVE_SNAPSHOT_SETTINGS.json
DAILY_SNAPSHOT_CONFIG.json
DAILY_SNAPSHOT_STATE.json
DAILY_SNAPSHOT_LOG.md

# Snapshot staging and Project Context Helper handoff artifacts.
SNAPSHOT_ACTIVE/
PROJECT_CONTEXT_HELPER/
PROJECT_CONTEXT_INDEX.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AutoExeBuilder
#
# Preserve authored build configuration and source specifications.
# Ignore generated build output and generated build manifests.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
auto_exe_output/
EXE_BUILD_MANIFEST.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ReadmeBuilder
#
# Generated drafts are disposable.
# Real README.md files remain trackable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
README_DRAFT.md
README_ANALYSIS.md
README_BUILDER_MANIFEST.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ReleaseNoteBuilder
#
# Generated drafts/manifests are disposable.
# Final CHANGELOG.md and RELEASE_NOTES.md remain trackable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CHANGELOG_DRAFT.md
RELEASE_MANIFEST.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared self-updater artifacts
#
# Keep updater source, release metadata, signatures, and trust anchors.
# Ignore downloaded/staged replacement payloads.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
updates/
apply_update.bat
staged_update.exe
download.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AirGapped-Web portable backups
#
# This is the distinctive generated backup filename.
# Do not globally ignore JSON, HTML, ZIP, records/, or archive content.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
airgapped-web-backup-*.json

# ==================================================
# 3. PROJECT-SCOPED RUNTIME AND PRIVATE DATA
# ==================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 02_Execution
#
# Keep framework configuration, stimuli, source, and published evidence.
# Ignore the execution updater's local preference file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/02_Execution/settings.json

# ==================================================
# 4. NATIVE APIs
# ==================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 94_Native_API's
#
# Versioned implementations, test vectors, fixtures, and documentation
# remain trackable. Global development-artifact rules cover caches.
# No blanket API output/data exclusions are introduced.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ==================================================
# 5. IDENTITY TOOLS
# ==================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 95_Identity_Tools
#
# Covers main, LTS-2028, and nested runtime data locations.
# Do not ignore the biometrics/, packages/, vault/, reports/, or
# vendor/ implementation directories themselves.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/95_Identity_Tools/**/data/

# Keyrings, device keys, and plaintext passphrase artifacts.
/95_Identity_Tools/**/keyring.json
/95_Identity_Tools/**/device_key.json
/95_Identity_Tools/**/*_passphrase.txt

# Sealed identity records and identity packages.
# Retained globally because custom output paths can leave the project.
*.identity
*.ibp

# Demo packages created outside the normal runtime data directory.
/95_Identity_Tools/**/DEMO_DO_NOT_USE_*/

# Synthetic capture artifacts.
/95_Identity_Tools/**/*.brvid

# ==================================================
# 6. BRISARTOS
# ==================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 96_Operating_System
#
# Keep kernel, host, storage, modules, extensions, schemas, tests,
# ROM source, and authored configuration trackable.
# Do not translate virtual filesystem paths into speculative host
# ignore rules: /system inside the OS is not necessarily a repo path.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# System API module runtime storage.
/96_Operating_System/**/module_data/

# Legacy/current-working-directory runtime storage at archive root.
/module_data/

# Host-side temporary replacement files.
/96_Operating_System/**/*.brisart-tmp

# Generated boot/floppy images.
/96_Operating_System/**/*.img
/96_Operating_System/**/*.vfd

# ==================================================
# 7. ENCRYPTION RESEARCH
# ==================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 97_Encryption
#
# Intentionally preserved:
#   results/
#   research_test_results.csv
#   research_test_results.json
#   research_test_results.md
#   research_test_config.json
#   known-answer vectors and test fixtures
#   security documentation and audio documentation
#
# No blanket results/, reports/, JSON, CSV, or transcript exclusions.
# Global bytecode/cache/private-key rules still apply.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ==================================================
# 8. TOOLING PROJECTS
# ==================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BrisartAI
#
# Ignore named runtime databases and designated generated stores.
# Do not ignore the engine's source packages, tests, or documentation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/98_Tooling/BrisartAI/conversation_memory.sqlite3
/98_Tooling/BrisartAI/session_memory.sqlite3
/98_Tooling/BrisartAI/brisart_ai_index.sqlite3

/98_Tooling/BrisartAI/exports/
/98_Tooling/BrisartAI/archive_exports/
/98_Tooling/BrisartAI/knowledge_exports/

/98_Tooling/BrisartAI/models/
/98_Tooling/BrisartAI/downloads/

/98_Tooling/BrisartAI/plugins/cache/
/98_Tooling/BrisartAI/crawl_cache/
/98_Tooling/BrisartAI/web_cache/
/98_Tooling/BrisartAI/scan_cache/

# Project-local operational logs, not research logs elsewhere.
/98_Tooling/BrisartAI/logs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Entitle
#
# These are the runtime directories defined by entitle/paths.py.
# Keep entitle/records.py, report.py, tracking/, examples/, tests/,
# vendor/, and documentation trackable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/98_Tooling/Entitle/entitlements/
/98_Tooling/Entitle/records/
/98_Tooling/Entitle/reports/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AirGapped-Web
#
# Keep authored site assets, registry content, records, HTML, CSS,
# JavaScript, and intentionally imported archival material trackable.
#
# Browser-local state is not a repository file.
# Portable backup JSON is covered in the shared-artifact section.
# Site-export ZIP files are not globally ignored: they may be
# intentional preservation artifacts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CanonSync
#
# Keep canonsync.config.json and canon/ master files trackable.
# Timestamped *.bak files are covered by the global backup rule.
# Do not ignore synchronized .gitignore, .gitattributes,
# .editorconfig, or LICENSE files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ProjectContextHelper / ArchiveSnapshot / AutoExeBuilder /
# ReadmeBuilder / ReleaseNoteBuilder
#
# Their generated artifacts are consolidated in section 2.
# Do not duplicate per-machine settings rules at the file's end.
# Source, tests, constants, and documentation remain trackable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ==================================================
# 9. AIO LAUNCHER
# ==================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# aio-launcher-prerelease
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Private release-signing material.
# Keep signing scripts and public verification material trackable.
/aio-launcher-prerelease/signing/keys/

# Local application settings.
/aio-launcher-prerelease/user_settings.json
/aio-launcher-prerelease/user_settings.json.tmp
/aio-launcher-prerelease/user_settings.json.bak
/aio-launcher-prerelease/user_settings.invalid*.json

# Legacy settings location used by config/runtime.py.
/aio-launcher-prerelease/config/user_settings.json
/aio-launcher-prerelease/config/user_settings.json.tmp
/aio-launcher-prerelease/config/user_settings.json.bak
/aio-launcher-prerelease/config/user_settings.invalid*.json

# Local activity history.
/aio-launcher-prerelease/activity_log.json
/aio-launcher-prerelease/activity_log.json.tmp
/aio-launcher-prerelease/activity_log.json.bak

# Framework execution output.
/aio-launcher-prerelease/outputs/

# Distinctive run/autosave names can appear at custom output paths.
tfl_output_*.csv
tfl_autosave_*.csv

# ==================================================
# 10. OPTIONAL LOCAL-ONLY WORKSPACE
#
# Reserved convention for future manual/local work.
# These are policy additions, not claims that tools create them.
# Do not place source, published evidence, or archival originals here.
# ==================================================
/.local/
/.local-artifacts/
/.local-secrets/

# ==================================================
# 11. PRESERVATION BOUNDARIES
#
# Intentionally no blanket exclusions for:
#
#   03_WIP/
#   04_Documentation/
#   05_Framework_Development/
#   06_Curriculum/
#   07_Podcast/
#   99_Admin/
#   audio/
#   docs/
#   tests/
#   fixtures/
#   vectors/
#   results/
#
# Also intentionally no global exclusions for:
#
#   *.md / *.txt / *.json / *.csv / *.sql
#   *.pdf / *.docx / *.xlsx / *.pptx
#   *.mp3 / *.m4a / *.wav / *.flac
#   *.png / *.jpg / *.jpeg / *.svg / *.ico
#   *.zip / *.7z / *.tar / *.gz
#   *.lock / *.spec / *.crt / *.cer / *.pub
#
# Private student records, participant data, and unpublished research
# require explicitly scoped storage rules once their actual paths
# are defined. Do not hide authored curriculum or evidence by guessing.
#
# ==================================================
# 12. CANONSYNC MANAGED BLOCK
#
# CanonSync's managed content belongs between its actual markers.
# Review any injected rules against the preservation boundaries above.
# Later matching patterns can change earlier ignore decisions.
